{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1557350-locust-manna-plague-and-other-charms","id":1557350,"title":"Locust Manna Plague and other Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-06T12:22:10-08:00","id":1557350,"title":"Locust Manna Plague and other Charms","content":"Does the 3E version of Locust Manna Plague only counts as food or does it count as food and water like the 2E version?<br /> <br /> When using Ultimate Darkness Internalization, can the Infernal still use Sorcery?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T13:38:57-08:00","id":1557352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1557350-locust-manna-plague-and-other-charms#post1557350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the 3E version of Locust Manna Plague only counts as food or does it count as food and water like the 2E version?</div> </div> </div> </div>It only refers to providing food.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When using Ultimate Darkness Internalization, can the Infernal still use Sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not say that they cannot.<br /> <br /> I believe the idea that circles of sorcery and necromancy are incompatible is no longer part of this Edition, so that aspect of the Charm seems to go with it.<br /> <br /> Presumably the main reason to ever transform back is any negatives from being undead.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T15:25:40-08:00","id":1557354,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your answer!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-08T03:11:21-08:00","id":1557372,"title":"","content":"Does the fog of Demonic Fog Shroud count as liquid for the purpose of using other Charms such as Ichor Flux Tendrils or Tainted Tide Malison?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T02:23:57-08:00","id":1557539,"title":"","content":"Does Psychic Surge Exertion applies its Strength to telekinetic attacks or only attacks with weapons held with telekinesis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T21:49:11-08:00","id":1557576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1557350-locust-manna-plague-and-other-charms?p=1557352#post1557352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It only refers to providing food.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that that's what the book says, but I'm not sure how the Infernal's cultists are supposed to survive while they're turning all the land into hell-desert if the locusts don't provide for their water needs. RAW you're right but I'd let them have the water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1557350-locust-manna-plague-and-other-charms?p=1557539#post1557539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the fog of Demonic Fog Shroud count as liquid for the purpose of using other Charms such as Ichor Flux Tendrils or Tainted Tide Malison?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scientifically, fog is an aerosol, a suspension of tiny water droplets in the air. Mystically, it's a Charm that evokes Kimbery and can be a vehicle for Spiteful Sea Tincture. I'd say it's liquid enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1557350-locust-manna-plague-and-other-charms?p=1557372#post1557372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Psychic Surge Exertion applies its Strength to telekinetic attacks or only attacks with weapons held with telekinesis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't it apply to (withering) telekinetic attacks? The key doesn't specify any requirements for the attack aside from &quot;withering attack roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also it really seems like the Charm is designed to favor direct telekinetic attack over telekinesis-wielded weapons, since (if I'm reading right) even Tool-Transcending Constructs doesn't mitigate that -3 penalty (since you're not relying &quot;solely&quot; on telekinesis if you're using a weapon to attack)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T03:47:48-08:00","id":1557587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1557350-locust-manna-plague-and-other-charms?p=1557576#post1557576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why wouldn't it apply to (withering) telekinetic attacks? The key doesn't specify any requirements for the attack aside from &quot;withering attack roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also it really seems like the Charm is designed to favor direct telekinetic attack over telekinesis-wielded weapons, since (if I'm reading right) even Tool-Transcending Constructs doesn't mitigate that -3 penalty (since you're not relying &quot;solely&quot; on telekinesis if you're using a weapon to attack)</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked because the text mentions that the damage of the base Mind-Hand Manipulation doesn't include the Infernal's Strength. But it would also make sense for the Key to modify this.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T08:43:12-08:00","id":1557602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1557350-locust-manna-plague-and-other-charms?p=1557587#post1557587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked because the text mentions that the damage of the base Mind-Hand Manipulation doesn't include the Infernal's Strength. But it would also make sense for the Key to modify this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but the key says &quot;effective Strength&quot; and also nothing else in MHM uses your <i>actual</i> Strength anyway. Telekinetic attacks just use WP instead of Intelligence for some reason (seems like the damage from max WP works out the same as a light weapon with max Strength though), I've no idea why.<br /> <br /> You're hitting them with physical force, so as far as I'm concerned there's an &quot;effective Strength&quot; buried in the math even if the text doesn't call it that. Hit harder, more damage. You could argue about whether this is strictest RAW, but in my eyes the intent of the key is clear enough -- IMO it would be silly if you could hit harder with a weapon but not with direct force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T22:54:17-08:00","id":1557641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1557350-locust-manna-plague-and-other-charms?p=1557576#post1557576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure how the Infernal's cultists are supposed to survive while they're turning all the land into hell-desert if the locusts don't provide for their water needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would not be out of theme for Charms drawing on the nature of Cecylene for the answer to that question to be &quot;with difficulty&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-15T18:05:50-08:00","id":1557662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1557350-locust-manna-plague-and-other-charms?p=1557641#post1557641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it would not be out of theme for Charms drawing on the nature of Cecylene for the answer to that question to be &quot;with difficulty&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, it wouldn't. It also wouldn't be out of theme for the locusts to provide water needs, considering they did just that in 2e -- the 2e version explicitly described the Charm as channeling Cecelyne's hypocrisy over her desert nature.<br /> <br /> I think the water makes sense because Cecelyne wants worshipers, not desiccated corpses. The point isn't for people to die, the point is to make them dependent on you. Your prospective cultists have a lot less motivation to stay in your Holy Land Infliction if there's no water-equivalent available there.<br /> <br /> I don't know for sure what the 3e writers' intent was, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T03:41:29-08:00","id":1557672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1557350-locust-manna-plague-and-other-charms?p=1557662#post1557662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your prospective cultists have a lot less motivation to stay in your Holy Land Infliction if there's no water-equivalent available there.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think there's a degree to which worshippers might be put in the position of remaining for higher priorities than concern over deprivation, if not where struggling within it for the sake of their devotion is part of the point, I can see the potential synergy between the Infernal being able to desecrate a land and then bestowing sustenance on a select few.<br /> <br /> Likewise, in comparing the writing of the Second Edition Charm to the Third and how they represent writing styles across Editions, I must recognise how the latter might have gone for something to get the point of providing general sustenance across without feeling the need for exactly precise language.<br /> <br /> In the end, I guess it comes down to how somebody wants to play it, and that it's not ruinous if the locusts suffice to provide for somebody's basic needs. I would still be inclined to an interpretation of it being a food source from which you won't suffer dehydration, but likewise won't feel satisfyingly parched by.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T06:03:37-08:00","id":1558018,"title":"","content":"Do you think an Infernal could use Mind-Hand manipulation to move the floating platform created with Crystalline Pattern Expansion if she's actually standing on said platform?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T12:00:24-08:00","id":1558026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1557350-locust-manna-plague-and-other-charms?p=1558018#post1558018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think an Infernal could use Mind-Hand manipulation to move the floating platform created with Crystalline Pattern Expansion if she's actually standing on said platform?</div> </div> </div> </div>While Mind-Hand Manipulation allows one to technically levitate things, it does so on a logic of extending the equivalent of a spectral limb that is capable of performing physical feats with atypical traits.<br /> <br /> On that basis, I would regard it as following the same logic of trying to move a non-floating platform by lifting a thing you are currently standing on with your own arms.<br /> <br /> Maybe it can be stunted every once in a while, but not an essential characteristic of those Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T12:18:43-08:00","id":1558027,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I have to agree that if you can't move the platform by physical means, telekinesis won't help you because it <i>is</i> a physical means.<br /> <br /> Crystalline Pattern Expansion doesn't explicitly say it can't be moved, but it's &quot;stationary&quot; and there are rules for breaking it but no rules for moving it, so I would conclude you indeed cannot move it.<br /> <br /> An expansion Charm (or key I guess) that allowed you to move constructs with MHM would make sense, I guess? Or something akin to 2e's Ascendant Objectivity Stance (damn I love that Charm name) if you just want to fly around. &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-14T23:02:11-08:00","id":1558338,"title":"","content":"If Mind-Hand Manipulation counts as limbs, could it be used to swing from tree to tree or building to building? Or as stilts to walk at Short range of the ground? Especially with Tools Transcending Construct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-15T10:50:28-08:00","id":1558343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1557350-locust-manna-plague-and-other-charms?p=1558338#post1558338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Mind-Hand Manipulation counts as limbs, could it be used to swing from tree to tree or building to building? Or as stilts to walk at Short range of the ground? Especially with Tools Transcending Construct?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Tool-Transcending Constructs would allow both of those, but the base Charm effect wouldn't. I don't think it literally works as if the &quot;mental limbs&quot; (perhaps not the best choice of words) were actually connected to the Infernal physically in that way -- pulling on a tree limb with telekinesis doesn't typically pull the user closer, but TTC can certainly emulate a grappling hook or stilts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}